{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation","id":958898,"title":"Celestial: The Reclamation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-27T14:56:12-07:00","id":958898,"title":"Celestial: The Reclamation","content":"<b>\u201c<u>Celestial: The Reclamation</u></b><br /> You were a god once--a Celestial. You were an Olympian sitting on your golden throne high atop your mountain, maintaining order in the world. You were a Deva sitting in your shining palace in the Heavens, passing judgment and bringing balance to the cycle of life. You were a Grigori flying high in the skies, teaching and guiding humanity towards a brighter future on behalf of Heaven. The world was once bright and full of possibilities--and then you fucked it all up.<br /> <br /> Your selfish and petty actions led to the creation of a child which overthrew the gods from their mountain; you're wasteful and negligent focus caused you to burn through your merit and you fell from your shining palaces in the heavens; you became distracted, eventually shirking your duties and bringing forth the great flood which nearly destroyed the world and forever banned you from your place in Heaven. You were a god once--immortal, all-powerful, and all but invincible\u2026but now you walk in the modern nights a mere shadow of your former self. This is a World of Darkness, and it's YOUR FAULT. You move across the planet now, hunted by creatures that once feared and worshipped you, trying desperately to pick up the pieces of your former glory all in the quest of that one seemingly impossible goal\u2026redemption.<br /> <br /> <u>Celestial</u>, a game of sorrow and lost majesty, where fallen gods seek reclamation: a way to right their wrongs and put the world the way it once was.\u201d<br /> <br /> A fan made game for the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> An idea I first posted in the fan-made splat display thread by ZealousChristian24, and due to the very positive response I got for it, I decided to throw it out there\u2026<br /> <br /> Looking for opinions, ideas, and things fans of the CoD want in a game about fallen god-like beings (because this is first and foremost a game for fans of the CoD), and others who would like to help develop this project and see if it is actually worth developing\u2026<br /> <br /> Inspirational material includes Literature like Neil Gaiman\u2019s <u>American Gods</u>; video games like <i>From Dust</i> and <i>Dark Souls</i>; and films like <i>The Green Mile</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 09-02-2016, 06:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:57:08-07:00","id":958899,"title":"","content":"X-Splat--<br /> <b><u>Regnum</u></b><br /> The origins of a Celestial, and the domain from which they draw power, they are as follows:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Madriax:</i></b> The Celestials of the Heavens, the All Seeing. Human legend recalls them as Indra, Thoth, Lao Zi, and Raziel. Even now as they walk the modern nights as shadows of what they once were, their preternatural powers of awareness are unmatched. Their symbol is the Eye of Providence.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Caosga:</i></b> The Celestials of Earth, the All Mighty. Mythology recalls them as Poseidon, Amurru, Thor, and the Thunderbird. Boasting power over the elements, even in their weakened state few can hope to match them for raw power. Their symbol is the occult symbol of the Earth and Power</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Cicle:</i></b> The Celestials of the Mysteries, The Travelers of the Planes. Mortal religion recalls them as Loki, Anansi, Hermes, and Coyote. Tricksters and travelers of multiple dimensions, even now in the darker modern nights they possess the uncanny ability to travel almost anywhere they please. Their symbol is the Traveler\u2019s Seal.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Malpirgi:</i></b> The Celestials of Life, the Creators. Ancient tradition remembers them as Amun, Saule, Aphrodite, and Inanna. Despite not being what they once were, many would be jealous for their powers over the affairs of mortals as well as their strange demiurgic abilities. Their symbol is a burning heart within the Star of Creation.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Teloah:</i></b> The Celestials of Death, the Destroyers. Human folklore might paint them as Azrael, Hades, the Baron Samedi, and Anubis. Not just lords over the dead and annihilators, but also hailed as protectors and guardians against malevolent forces\u2014even in their now weakened state, most wouldn\u2019t be able to challenge them in their chosen domains. Their symbol is a skull sat atop the Symbol of the Underworld.</div><br /> Y-Splat--<br /> <b><u>Creed</u></b><br /> The faction a Celestial chooses for itself; groups who ban together under common ideals in how to reclaim their destinies based on their own personal beliefs and their fuzzy memories of their past lives:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Titanes: </i></b>Other wise known as the Elder Gods</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>The Grigorian Choir: </i></b>Otherwise known as the Watchers</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>The Fallen Devas: </i></b>Otherwise known as Divinities</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>The Defiled Shrine: </i></b>Otherwise known as Totems,</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>The Descended Masters:</i></b> Otherwise known as the New Gods</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b><i>Outer Gods:</i></b> Otherwise known as Horrors</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 08-27-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:59:14-07:00","id":958902,"title":"","content":"I hate to say this, but you're gonna have a really hard time making a game about the gods when Scion has a Kickstarter next month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:12:35-07:00","id":958909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=958902#post958902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate to say this, but you're gonna have a really hard time making a game about the gods when Scion has a Kickstarter next month.</div> </div> </div> </div>You suppose so? No big deal if it is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:20:57-07:00","id":958914,"title":"","content":"you could perhaps take a look at Demon: the Return for some inspiration- it also shares the basic idea of ancient gods returning to the world, although through a different interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:26:49-07:00","id":958919,"title":"","content":"Im loving them splats!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:43:16-07:00","id":958923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=958919#post958919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im loving them splats!</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you do! Here's part of the Lexicon I've been building up: <br /> <b><i><u>Lexicon (work in progress)</u></i></b><br /> <br /> <b>Bodhi: </b>The level of understanding a Celestial possesses about themselves, their nature, their past sins, and how best to go about reclaiming their destiny; the Celestial Integrity trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Choshek:</b> A corruptive and infectious darkness born of the chaos caused by the misdeeds of the Celestials in ages past fermented in the energies of the <i>Welkin</i>\u2014capable of infecting places; objects; and even people, it can nullify Celestial powers and cause tremendous damage not only to their <i>Vessels</i>, but their <i>Manifestations</i> as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Cintamani: </b>Strange crystalline stones, also known as \u2018Baetylus,\u2019 with strange and unpredictable properties which materialize in the <i>Welkin</i> from unused potential energy and fall to the mortal plane.<br /> <br /> <b>Constellation: </b>A group of two or more Celestials working towards common ends. <br /> <br /> <b>Creed: </b>One of six factions Celestials join in response to the broken world and how to go about reclaiming their destiny.<br /> <br /> <b>Designs:</b> Powers which Celestials enact through their <i>Raptures</i> to subtly influence creatures and world events, the influence of which can grow more far-reaching and profound by tapping into the <i>Welkin</i>. <br /> <br /> <b>Imperium: </b>The measure of a Celestial\u2019s power\u2014as well as how far and intimately it may influence the world around it; the Celestial power level and supernatural tolerance trait. <br /> <br /> <b>Keres: </b>A collective term for the former servants and enforcers, and now sworn enemies, of the Celestials who are prone to using <i>Choshek</i> to their advantage.<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>The \u2018true form\u2019 of a Celestial, and the embodiment of their power that maintains its integrity by remaining attached to a mortal <i>Vessel</i>, and can only be made manifest in the mundane world under very specific circumstances. <br /> <br /> <b>Nectar: </b>The foodstuffs of Celestials; <i>Odum</i> energy harvested from mortal concepts and ideals in action. <br /> <br /> <b>Odum: </b>Otherwise known as the Odic force, or the <i>\u00e9lan vital</i>\u2014the raw energy through which Celestials enact the powers\u2014the Celestial energy trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Outer Darkness: </b>The realm just outside the edge of the <i>Welkin</i>; the Great Void<br /> <br /> <b>Phenomena: </b>The impressive otherworldly abilities unique to Celestials, which can be enhanced by tapping into the <i>Welkin</i>, and come in two categories\u2014<i>Revelations</i> and <i>Designs</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Rapture: </b> The gigantic \u2018shadow\u2019 cast by a Celestial\u2019s <i>Manifestation</i> which influences events and behavior of all things that fall under it; through this \u2018shadow\u2019 Celestials may enact <i>Designs</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Regnum:</b> One of five origins determining what \u201ctype\u201d of higher being a Celestial is and the types of powers they lean towards.<br /> <br /> <b>Revelations:</b> The \u2018up close and personal\u2019 powers in a Celestial\u2019s arsenal, limited in scope and duration (affecting only the immediate environment), but blatantly supernatural and spectacular to behold. Can be truly earth shaking when tapped into the power of the <i>Welkin</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanctuary: </b>A safe haven for a Celestial as well as those in her <i>Constellation</i>. <br /> <br /> <b>Vessel: </b>A recently deceased mortal body that a Celestial has attached its <i>Manifestation</i> to in order to maintain itself, as well as interact with the mortal world.<br /> <br /> <b>Welkin:</b> The original abode of the Celestials; a higher plane of existence that connected all the realms in the World of Darkness together and ensured their vitality and potential in ages long past, but now lies in ruins. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T16:02:56-07:00","id":958935,"title":"","content":"do you have any ideas about what was the original dive realm the celestials came from? and where is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:42:21-07:00","id":959056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=958935#post958935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do you have any ideas about what was the original dive realm the celestials came from? and where is it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, as noted in the Lexicon, the Realm they hail from is the <i>Welkin</i>, and it is literally everywhere. It once connected all the planes of existence in the WoD, but due to the infighting of the Celestials, it crumbled and fell to disuse. <br /> <br /> And, like a body that suffered damage to its nervous system, the various realms became disjointed from one another, and fell into decay, thus resulting in the WoD as it is known today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T20:42:55-07:00","id":959057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=958914#post958914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you could perhaps take a look at Demon: the Return for some inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll definitely look into that, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T20:55:15-07:00","id":960838,"title":"","content":"I love this a lot so far. Keep it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T23:18:57-07:00","id":961473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=960838#post960838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this a lot so far. Keep it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, glad you like it, just for you then:<br /> <br /> <b>Y-splat Expansion/Explanation: </b><br /> <br /> Celestials memories of their past are fuzzy and non-substantial at best. What was once a mighty entity dwelling in dimensions of existence beyond human comprehension now forced to squeeze its consciousness into the meat of a puny mortal frame just to remain coherent. Very few things of its past squeeze through the consciousness of the Celestial's vessel...but a few things go through as feelings, images, and visions with highly metaphorical imagery...what few pieces a Celestial can gather of what it once was is used as its foundation into how to right its past wrongs and reclaim its destiny as a higher being.<br /> <br /> These foundations are what has served as the basis of the five Creeds which Celestials choose to become a part of, each one drawing from certain mortal religions and philosophies (for every religion ultimately revolves around the suffering of the world and how to mitigate it, and as far as Celestials are concerned, mortal religion is based on THEM). Each Creed is governed by a specific overseer which coordinates the Celestials of their own Pantheon worldwide, each revolves around a specific theme, and each draws Nectar from specific human concepts--<ul><li><b><u>Titanes</u></b>: Otherwise known as the Elder Gods, these beings find resonance with the ancient giants, the elemental spirits, and thundering lords of heaven from many old religions. These Celestials believe their primary failing was a misuse of Power--Whether they took it for granted and became complacent enough to be overthrown, or they abused it to the point that those beneath them rose up, or they simply grew overconfident and were overcome is up for debate, but all of them agree that to reclaim their former existence they must amass the power they once had.<ul><li>Their theme is Personal Greatness</li> <li>The Celestial governing the Creed is known as the Tyrant</li> <li>They draw their philosophy from such religious beliefs as Ancient Greek, Babylonian, and even more modern philosophers like Nietzsche</li> <li>The Concepts they harvest Nectar from are such things as Competition, Strength, and Reaching for the Impossible</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b><u>The Grigorian Choir</u></b>: Otherwise known as the Watchers, these beings find resonance with the fallen angels, beings of light, and djinns of Abrahamic myth. These Celestials believe their primary failing had been in succumbing to corruption, and in turn, letting the world that was supposed to be their ward fall to corruption as well. To reclaim the world that once was, these Celestials believe that they must restore the good that was drained from it many eons ago.<ul><li>Their theme is Virtue</li> <li>The Celestial in charge is known as the Metatron</li> <li>They draw their philosophies from mainly Monotheistic faiths, including lesser known books and mystic off-branches such as the Kabbalah</li> <li>The Concepts they receive Nectar from are such things as Charity, Forgiveness, and Healing</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b><u>The Fallen Devas</u></b>: Otherwise known as Divinities, these Celestials find themselves most like the devas, demons, and spiritual beings of Eastern religions. They believe their primary failing had been in losing touch with their inner self, losing balance and thus throwing the world itself into disorder. To reclaim their place in the heavens, they believe that they must restore balance to the world and the creatures within it.<ul><li>Their theme is Order</li> <li>The Celestial who oversees their activities is known as the Bodhisattva</li> <li>They draw their philosophies from a melting pot of eastern philosophies such as Hinduism, Buddhism, Taoism, etc.</li> <li>The Concepts they draw Nectar from are such things as Karma, Detachment, and Self-Control</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b><u>The Defiled Shrine</u></b>: Otherwise known as Totems, These Celestials find the most in common with Animistic philosophies from around the world. They believe their primary failing had been in letting too much control fall over Nature, and thus the spirit of the world grew sick. To reclaim the fallen world, they believe they must remove the illusion of control brought on by modern times, and let Nature rule as it once did.<ul><li>Their theme is Freedom</li> <li>Though they tend to avoid titles, the Celestial hailed first (especially when dealing with other Celestial groups) is referred to as the Alpha</li> <li>They draw their philosophies from such things a s Shintoism, various Native American beliefs, and shamanic practices</li> <li>The Concepts they procure Nectar from are such things as Growth, Tradition, and Intuition</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b><u>The Descended Masters</u></b>: Otherwise known as the New Gods, these Celestials don't really seem to fit anywhere, and seek to reinvent themselves in a new light. These odd beings believe that whatever they once were had failed due to an inability to evolve or change with the times. To heal the world, they feel they must become something entirely new to the world of spirituality.<ul><li>Their theme is Progress</li> <li>The group who govern the Creed are known as the Wise Ones</li> <li>They draw their philosophies from New Age sources; a pick and mix of whatever they believe works</li> <li>The Concepts they gather Nectar from are such things as Advancement, Artistic Expression, and Originality</li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><b><u>Outer Gods</u></b>: Otherwise known as Horrors, these Celestials have for whatever reason, given up on reclaiming their original place and now seek to destroy the world. Their reasons vary, but the most popular one is that the world is just too broken...too dark to be worth saving. A new, better world must be made, and to do that, the World of Darkness must be smashed to atoms.<ul><li>Their theme is Death</li> <li>Their is no formal leadership among the outer gods, though they may form small groups dedicated to destroying the world in a specific way</li> <li>Their philosophy is very personal, but if one had to choose, they draw many of their ideas from Doomsday cults from around the globe</li> <li>The Concepts they gain Nectar from are such things as Blood Sacrifice, Enslavement, and Genocide</li> </ul></li> </ul>Haven't quite figured what the benefits of each Creed would be yet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 09-10-2016, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T08:36:47-07:00","id":961675,"title":"","content":"Have you considered each Creed giving a free dot in an appropriate specialty? Just a suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12243-dreaming-cat","name":"Dreaming Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T02:04:54-07:00","id":962163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaming Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=961675#post961675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered each Creed giving a free dot in an appropriate specialty? Just a suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of specific occult practices, but that sounds like an interesting idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T03:27:32-07:00","id":962177,"title":"","content":"I am certainly interested in this fansplat, especially as I am going something vaguely similar (Demigod: the Empyrean). From what I've seen so far of Celestial, it is kind of like the two mirror each other, with demigods being people whose souls have been made a host for a luminous, divine thing and Celestials being luminous, divine things being forced to live as people in a mortal world. I shall most certainly watch with eager anticipation. If you're agreeable, I would be happy to help out a bit, although i don't know how much I'll be able to do at the moment, what with going back to college and stuff.<br /> <br /> Keep up the good work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T03:30:46-07:00","id":962178,"title":"","content":"One question, though. What is the difference between nectar and Odum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:03:44-07:00","id":962184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=962178#post962178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question, though. What is the difference between nectar and Odum?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of like the difference between Tass and Mana in <i>Mage</i> -- Odum is the raw energy itself, while Nectar is a medium through which it can be gathered, distributed, and (most importantly) stored for later use. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:10:54-07:00","id":962190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=962177#post962177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're agreeable, I would be happy to help out a bit, although i don't know how much I'll be able to do at the moment, what with going back to college and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be honored for your help! I was hoping to get more people on board...<br /> <br /> Honestly, I had been worried that you might be offended at my idea for being too close to your own, but I'm glad you like it so far! <br /> <br /> And, I will definitely need help in fleshing out the powers of the Celestials--I'm a pretty good idea guy, but when it comes to mechanics, I stumble quite a bit. <br /> <br /> I would also be interested in helping you with your project, once I find the time to read through it a bit more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:28:39-07:00","id":962195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=962184#post962184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's kind of like the difference between Tass and Mana in <i>Mage</i> -- Odum is the raw energy itself, while Nectar is a medium through which it can be gathered, distributed, and (most importantly) stored for later use.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T04:34:36-07:00","id":962197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=962190#post962190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be honored for your help! I was hoping to get more people on board...<br /> <br /> Honestly, I had been worried that you might be offended at my idea for being too close to your own, but I'm glad you like it so far!<br /> <br /> And, I will definitely need help in fleshing out the powers of the Celestials--I'm a pretty good idea guy, but when it comes to mechanics, I stumble quite a bit.<br /> <br /> I would also be interested in helping you with your project, once I find the time to read through it a bit more...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In order:<br /> <br /> Thank you, and I'd be happy to.<br /> <br /> Not at all! After all, I don't own the concept of gods or anything ridiculous like that. And I have to say, I think that flavour-wise yours is probably more interesting. For demigod one of the nagging doubts I've had about it is that it's too bland. However, I think that the two games can coexist fairly happily. After all, as I said, it's like Celestials and demigods are coming at divinity from opposite direction: Celestials have been there and failed and demigods are trying to get there but have no idea what it's like.* I think that if the two got to talking they would probably either blow each other off the face of the earth with Miracles and Revelations for respective blasphemy or get on like a temple on fire.<br /> <br /> I think I'm kind of in the same boat as you there, to a degree. Most of my mechanics come from pinching buts and pieces of other games and stuff. i'll do what I can, though.<br /> <br /> If you could, I would be eternally in your debt. Thank you very much for the offer. It means a lot to me.<br /> <br /> *That's not to say that they originate from the same source, were/are working towards the same thing or are even connected at all, beyond a shared connection to the concept of divinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 09-02-2016, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T05:05:34-07:00","id":962203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=962197#post962197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think that the two games can coexist fairly happily. After all, as I said, it's like Celestials and demigods are coming at divinity from opposite direction: Celestials have been there and failed and demigods are trying to get there but have no idea what it's like.* I think that if the two got to talking they would probably either blow each other off the face of the earth with Miracles and Revelations for respective blasphemy or get on like a temple on fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>What a novel idea! <br /> <br /> I've got some work to do myself, but I'm officially excited!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T05:48:40-07:00","id":962209,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Designs: are they simply a kind of passive 'aura' around the Celestial, constantly and subtly shaping the world to his desires or does the character have to 'turn it on'? Does the Celestial actually <i>choose </i>what their Designs do, or is it a kind of subconscious thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T12:24:26-07:00","id":962438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=962209#post962209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question about Designs: are they simply a kind of passive 'aura' around the Celestial, constantly and subtly shaping the world to his desires or does the character have to 'turn it on'? Does the Celestial actually <i>choose </i>what their Designs do, or is it a kind of subconscious thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Designs are active powers the Celestial chooses to enact through their Raptures, which in many ways are like an aura (a very, very, very large aura) generated by their Manifestation. <br /> <br /> Designs are always made through conscious effort on part of the Celestial. However, their Rapture is always on and is always subtly influencing the world around them in a very passive way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:34:18-07:00","id":966243,"title":"","content":"I like what you're doing with this fansplat. I can't wait to read more.<br /> <br /> However, I do have a question: what happens if a Celestial's Vessel is destroyed? Do they simply find a new one and start over again or do they retain their memories from the last Vessel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10600-howlingseas23","name":"HowlingSeas23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:02:35-07:00","id":966756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HowlingSeas23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=966243#post966243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what you're doing with this fansplat. I can't wait to read more.<br /> <br /> However, I do have a question: what happens if a Celestial's Vessel is destroyed? Do they simply find a new one and start over again or do they retain their memories from the last Vessel?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you! <br /> <br /> And to answer your question, losing a Vessel is always traumatic. Though the Celestial will keep its memories, in claiming a new Vessel it will essentially start at level one again, and due to the disconnect of being in an unfamiliar body it will find rising to higher levels more difficult. <br /> <br /> Not to say destroying a Celestial's Vessel is an easy thing to do...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T08:23:02-07:00","id":966766,"title":"","content":"Here's a question for everybody! <br /> <br /> What would you picture the skull icon for Celestial to look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:35:50-07:00","id":966861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=966766#post966766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question for everybody! <br /> <br /> What would you picture the skull icon for Celestial to look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Skull with a spiky halo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-u