 </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a combination of Saulott and ajf115's suggestions? They both sound cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a skull with burning eyes, and a halo of a spinning galaxy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T19:09:19-07:00","id":968308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=968056#post968056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, will Designs and Revelations be specific, singular powers similarly to Exploits, tiered ones like Disciplines, supernatural 'skills' like Arcana...?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I'm figuring it, Designs and Revelations will be related to each other in that both will fall under certain &quot;Spheres&quot; (as in &quot;sphere of influence').<br /> <br /> For example, there will be a &quot;<i>Sphere of Elements</i>&quot;, which will contain purviews like <i>Earth</i>, <i>Fire</i>, <i>Wind</i>, and <i>Water</i>. The purview of <i>Fire</i> in this sphere will allow the Celestial in question access to 'Revelations' which control fire, heat, and perhaps even lava (making the sky rain fire and lightning perhaps). While on the 'Design' side of things, the Celestial will be able to control fire in a more metaphorical way, like being ale to incite passion in a mob, kindling a fiery drive in a political movement, or striking a singular individual with a divine spark of creativity. The more power the Celestial powers into the effect, the more powerful the effect.<br /> <br /> By tapping into the power of the <i>Welkin</i>, a Celestial can ignite Revelations which can split land masses with volcanic explosions or setting a sea ablaze, and Designs which may incite world-spanning artistic movements and country-wide conflicts, or even perhaps something like helping a demiurge bring a promethean to life. Of course, tapping into the power of the <i>Welkin</i> always calls the attention of <b>Keres</b> (more on the nature of the <i>Welkin </i>and <i>Keres</i> later).<br /> <br /> The <b><i>Caosga</i></b> Celestials will be the most naturally gifted in the &quot;<i>Sphere of Elements</i>&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 09-12-2016, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T23:36:08-07:00","id":968393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=968308#post968308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I'm figuring it, Designs and Revelations will be related to each other in that both will fall under certain &quot;Spheres&quot; (as in &quot;sphere of influence').<br /> <br /> For example, there will be a &quot;<i>Sphere of Elements</i>&quot;, which will contain purviews like <i>Earth</i>, <i>Fire</i>, <i>Wind</i>, and <i>Water</i>. The purview of <i>Fire</i> in this sphere will allow the Celestial in question access to 'Revelations' which control fire, heat, and perhaps even lava (making the sky rain fire and lightning perhaps). While on the 'Design' side of things, the Celestial will be able to control fire in a more metaphorical way, like being ale to incite passion in a mob, kindling a fiery drive in a political movement, or striking a singular individual with a divine spark of creativity. The more power the Celestial powers into the effect, the more powerful the effect.<br /> <br /> By tapping into the power of the <i>Welkin</i>, a Celestial can ignite Revelations which can split land masses with volcanic explosions or setting a sea ablaze, and Designs which may incite world-spanning artistic movements and country-wide conflicts, or even perhaps something like helping a demiurge bring a promethean to life. Of course, tapping into the power of the <i>Welkin</i> always calls the attention of <b>Keres</b> (more on the nature of the <i>Welkin </i>and <i>Keres</i> later).<br /> <br /> The <b><i>Caosga</i></b> Celestials will be the most naturally gifted in the &quot;<i>Sphere of Elements</i>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> On another note, do you know the RPG Godbound? I think that there would be some material in there which would be very useful. There's a free version on DrivethruRPG that's got everything you really need to know and although it runs on the d20 system, a lot of the non-mechanical stuff would be pertinent, particularly the section on divine Gifts and the one on the shattered pieces of Heaven, abandoned and cast adrift within Uncreated Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:59:15-07:00","id":968520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=968297#post968297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How about a skull with burning eyes, and a halo of a spinning galaxy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Even better than what I was thinking of originally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10600-howlingseas23","name":"HowlingSeas23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:05:53-07:00","id":969129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=968393#post968393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> On another note, do you know the RPG Godbound? I think that there would be some material in there which would be very useful. There's a free version on DrivethruRPG that's got everything you really need to know and although it runs on the d20 system, a lot of the non-mechanical stuff would be pertinent, particularly the section on divine Gifts and the one on the shattered pieces of Heaven, abandoned and cast adrift within Uncreated Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just picked up the pdf, will be looking at that, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T00:22:57-07:00","id":969723,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm most definitely having trouble with is what Celestials would be struggling with.<br /> <br /> Mages have hubris, prometheans have torment, vampires have the beast, princesses have self-righteousness...<br /> <br /> I was thinking that personal vice would be a major stumbling block for most Celestials--it would increase their power but also twist them into their former problematic personalities, but I'm not so sure about that idea...<br /> <br /> What do you guys think would oppose the <i>Bodhi</i> of a Celestial?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 09-15-2016, 03:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:37:51-07:00","id":969758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=969723#post969723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I'm most definitely having trouble with is what Celestials would be struggling with.<br /> <br /> Mages have hubris, prometheans have torment, vampires have the beast, princesses have self-righteousness...<br /> <br /> I was thinking that personal vice would be a major stumbling block for most Celestials--it would increase their power but also twist them into their former problematic personalities, but I'm not so sure about that idea...<br /> <br /> What do you guys think would oppose the <i>Bodhi</i> of a Celestial?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps some kind of wilful ignorance? <i>Bodhi</i> is referred to as understanding of themselves and their place in the cosmos, but the truth of that could be a painful one. They would know <i>exactly</i> how far they have fallen and how hopeless the climb back up is. Perhaps the opposition to <i>B</i><i>odhi</i> could effectively be the horror of that truth, the fact that, ultimately, <i>the gods failed</i>, and they failed so badly that they were stripped of their crowns and thrones and cast down upon the earth, to walk among the ruins of their creation. Therefore, you lose <i>Bodhi</i> when you cannot accept this truth, and the fact that, no matter how hard it is, you must always do better. It's all too easy to forget your pain, to drown your sorrow in drink or work and forget both the pain and what must be done. That is when you lose <i>Bodhi</i>.<br /> <br /> Does that sound reasonable, or are your thoughts different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:26:30-07:00","id":969981,"title":"","content":"Taking what I said earlier even further, could Bodhi start low, and grant both benefits and curses as it raises? On one hand, you're more clear-sighted and determined, on the other, you see your own failure and ruin with the same clarity. Perhaps the Outer Gods could, in fact, be Celestials with <i>high</i> Bodhi, as they see what they must do, how far they have fallen and despair, railing at the world and wishing oblivion upon it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:48:45-07:00","id":969998,"title":"","content":"Pardon if it sounds like I'm kind of ripping from another series of games, but in my opinion, the flaw of the Solars in Exalted could be used for inspiration?<br /> <br /> Pretty much, the Solar Exalted were made to be the leaders and rulers over creation. When they cast down the Primordials/Yozis, the Yozis unleashed a Great Curse upon them that would cause their emotions to go entirely crazy once in awhile. During this time (known as Limit Break), the Solar will undergo a path of self-destructive actions that can be terrible for themselves and the people around them. Usually, the limit break coincides with the Solar's VIRTUE, aka what's called their Virtue Flaw.<br /> <br /> Just to give a couple of examples, here's one of the many Virtue Flaws for each of the four virtues in Exalted.<br /> <br /> Compassion<br /> <b>Heart of Tears: </b>The Solar can only cower and weep at all of the percieved injustices they've encountered. They cannot even defend against an attack while crying their eyes out.<br /> <br /> Valor<br /> <b>Unhesitating Rage: </b>The Character knows no fear or hestitation and will bully people to get her way. She will not reject ANY challenge, period. The character isn't completely suicidal to note, only if death is a possibility in the very short term will the character ever think of retreating.<br /> <br /> Conviction<br /> <b>Benevolent Tyrrany: </b>The Solar grows sick of the percieved stupidity about him and will not tolerate it anymore. They know what's best for others, and will respect no authority but his own and accept no compromises. They will try to persuade people to do as they say, and if that fails, then they'll use force.<br /> <br /> Temperance<br /> <b>Tenacious Paranoia: </b>The Solar becomes incredibly paranoid. No plan of theirs is safe nor are those near them. They become paralyzed by how much can ruin their desires and will work to make sure they can't be taken down. They also flatly don't trust people with their plans, and as such will not include any allies into them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:18:00-07:00","id":970546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=969981#post969981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking what I said earlier even further, could Bodhi start low, and grant both benefits and curses as it raises? On one hand, you're more clear-sighted and determined, on the other, you see your own failure and ruin with the same clarity. Perhaps the Outer Gods could, in fact, be Celestials with <i>high</i> Bodhi, as they see what they must do, how far they have fallen and despair, railing at the world and wishing oblivion upon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting thought...almost like depression itself is their greatest threat. The feeling of hopelessness, that they follow an impossible cause... <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","user":"hellovg","date":". 09-16-2016, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:22:03-07:00","id":970548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/958898-celestial-the-reclamation?p=969998#post969998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon if it sounds like I'm kind of ripping from another series of games, but in my opinion, the flaw of the Solars in Exalted could be used for inspiration?<br /> <br /> Pretty much, the Solar Exalted were made to be the leaders and rulers over creation. When they cast down the Primordials/Yozis, the Yozis unleashed a Great Curse upon them that would cause their emotions to go entirely crazy once in awhile. During this time (known as Limit Break), the Solar will undergo a path of self-destructive actions that can be terrible for themselves and the people around them. Usually, the limit break coincides with the Solar's VIRTUE, aka what's called their Virtue Flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...that's more in line with what I was thinking originally...but more along the lines that Celestials had to avoid falling back into bad habits...I'll think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T06:36:41-07:00","id":1141045,"title":"","content":"Working on a collaborative project with ajf115: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141041-empyrean-the-redemption-collaborative-fansplat\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1141041-empyrean-the-redemption-collaborative-fansplat\"> Empyrean: the Redemption [Collaborative fansplat] - Onyx Path Forums </a